      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like your partner might be experiencing a high blood sugar episode, which can cause excessive thirst, nausea, confusion, and even a sweet-smelling breath known as \"fruity\" odor. Getting them some water is a good start, but it's important to monitor their blood sugar level if you have access to a glucometer. Promptly contacting a healthcare professional or emergency services, if they're unresponsive, is crucial because high blood sugar can be life-threatening if left untreated. Let them rest but keep an eye on them until you can get professional help.",
